{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.desktop.tsbuildinfo",
    "target": "ES2022",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    /* Bundler mode — the same as tsconfig.app.json's, because the modules this
       reaches into are the same modules.

       There is NO `types` array, deliberately, and there was one until the mount
       slice's second half. It named `vite/client` and `node` because this project
       could not see `src/vite-env.d.ts`; it also, silently, hid every other
       ambient package — and the moment this project began compiling the whole
       application, `@types/dompurify`'s UMD namespace went missing and
       `security/xss-protection.ts` stopped compiling here while compiling
       perfectly in the web build. A difference between two CONFIGS reported as a
       difference between two EDITIONS is the one failure mode this project must
       not have, so the ambient environment is now identical to the app
       project's: no `types`, and the four `.d.ts` files in `include` below. */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": false,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false,
    "erasableSyntaxOnly": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": false,

    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      /* The edition seam, pointed at the DEVICE engine — the whole difference
         between this project and tsconfig.app.json. Any shared surface the
         desktop renderer mounts is compiled here against the port a file
         provides, so a component that only typechecks against DataService is a
         build error in this project rather than a discovery at run time. */
      "@data": ["./src/services/local/deviceDataPort.ts"],
      /* The mount slice's four seams, device halves. Layout is not mounted in
         this project yet — that is part 2 — but the halves themselves are
         compiled here against the contracts in `src/editions/`, which is what
         makes them substitutable rather than merely present. */
      "@chrome": ["./src/desktop/editions/chrome.tsx"],
      "@identity": ["./src/desktop/editions/identity.ts"],
      "@prefs-store": ["./src/desktop/editions/preferencesStore.ts"],
      "@telemetry": ["./src/desktop/editions/telemetry.ts"],
      "@session": ["./src/desktop/editions/session.ts"],
      "@service": ["./src/desktop/editions/service.ts"],
      "@wealthtracker/utils": ["./packages/utils/index.ts"],
      "@wealthtracker/utils/*": ["./packages/utils/*"],
      "@wealthtracker/types/*": ["./packages/types/*"],
      "@app-types/*": ["./src/types/*"]
    }
  },
  /* `src/desktop` and the AMBIENT DECLARATIONS, and nothing else of src: the
     renderer lives inside this repo's lint, typecheck and test roots on purpose
     (deviceDocument.ts's header gives the reason), and everything it reaches is
     compiled with it — which from the mount slice's second half is the whole
     application.

     The four `.d.ts` files are listed because a project's `include` is what
     brings ambient declarations in, and they are not otherwise reachable by an
     import: `DOMPurify`'s global namespace (security/xss-protection),
     `react-window-infinite-loader`'s missing types (VirtualizedList),
     `navigator.hapticFeedback` (useHapticFeedback) and `vite/client`'s
     `import.meta.env`. tsconfig.app.json gets all four from `include: ["src"]`.
     Without them this project reports six errors in shared modules that compile
     perfectly well in the web build, which is a difference between two configs
     rather than a difference between two editions — and this project exists to
     find the second kind. */
  "include": [
    "src/desktop",
    "src/vite-env.d.ts",
    "src/types/global.d.ts",
    "src/types/react-window-infinite-loader.d.ts",
    "src/types/external/regression.d.ts",
    "apps/desktop/vite.config.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["src/desktop/**/__tests__/**"]
}
